# tools/al/ales_wav_witness.rish — a bounded buffer of i16 PCM samples round-trips through the canonical RIFF/WAVE container,
# verify-before-trust (ALES215).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES215.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-130110_fill-ales215-lotus-wav-container.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/wire.rye (ALES0) — the same two-gate discipline (structure whole AND sample-aligned), now speaking the
# open RIFF/WAVE format the outside world already reads and writes, so every one of the 200-plus Lotus effects gains an
# export and an import through one bounded, asserted container.
#
# lotus/wav.rye encodes a bounded block of mono i16 PCM samples into the canonical 44-byte-header RIFF/WAVE layout and decodes
# it verify-before-trust. The selftest proves: the block round-trips byte-for-byte with its sample-rate field preserved; the
# header is exactly canonical; an empty buffer yields a valid 44-byte header; a data chunk one byte short of whole samples
# refuses PartialSample at the audio border; and every header corruption refuses by name. A byte container only — no real file
# opened, no DAC, no acoustic or electrical fact asserted, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_wav_witness.rish

say "ales-wav: Language EN — ALES215 opens a fresh Lotus family, the container: a bounded buffer of PCM samples encoded into the open RIFF/WAVE .wav layout another program will play, and decoded back verify-before-trust exactly as ALES0's wire proved its payload whole."
say "ales-wav: Style Radiant — one canonical 44-byte header, a single source of truth (RIFF · WAVE · fmt  · format · channels · rate · byte_rate · block_align · bits · data); every corruption refuses by name before a sample crosses."
say "ales-wav: Lens TAME — decoding is two independent gates, the size chain proving the container self-consistent and the audio border proving it sample-aligned so no torn half-sample reaches a timeline; the sample rate is a carried field not a real clock; siloed to lotus/, no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/wav"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/wav.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-wav: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/wav.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-wav: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-wav: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-wav' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-wav: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-wav line"

say "ales-wav: GREEN — a bounded buffer of i16 PCM samples round-trips byte-for-byte through the canonical RIFF/WAVE container proven whole and sample-aligned; the next Lotus rung can carry the stereo twin (channels 2, interleaved), or a render that runs an effect chain and writes the result."
